Rosalind, Nathaniel,<br />
<br />
Before Wednesday's call I want to settle what we are actually asking Marchw=
ood to commit to, because I think the obvious answer is the wrong one.<br /=
>
<br />
The obvious answer is: obtain the 2010 surprise examination, file the Form =
ADV-E, and we close. That fixes the year we examined and nothing else. The =
exposure here is structural. Marchwood's growth is acquisitive - they bough=
t two small books in 2009 and 2010 and they are looking at more. Every book=
 they buy arrives with its own advisory agreements and its own custody arra=
ngements. A remediation scoped to calendar 2010 puts us back here in three =
years with the same finding on different accounts.<br />
<br />
What I want in writing is an undertaking with no end date: the accounts mov=
e to a qualified custodian under an arrangement that does not give Marchwoo=
d withdrawal authority, the direct fee-debit practice stops, and the same t=
reatment is applied to anything they onboard or acquire in the future. If t=
hey will commit to that, the recommendation is to close on the undertaking =
rather than to refer.<br />
<br />
If we take the narrow remediation and the practice comes back after this co=
mpliance officer leaves, the record will show we closed with no findings.<b=
r />
